     1,
     "I thought the R file that Brandon included originally was very useful.\r<br>I&#39;ve attached it to this document.  (I hope that&#39;s OK.)\r<br>\r<br>-- Mike\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "\r<br>\r<br>On Sat, Feb 6, 2016 at 9:27 PM, Brandon Hurr &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">brando...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:\r<br>&gt; I&#39;m still working on getting them up somewhere but you can download them\r<br>&gt; from here as TalkMain.html\r<br>&gt; <a href=\"https://github.com/bhive01/2016-02-D-RUG-dplyr-II-talk\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/bhive01/2016-02-D-RUG-dplyr-II-talk&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792467557197000&amp;usg=AOvVaw27lTnDOs7eRGNCT4Ax93m2\">https://github.com/bhive01/2016-02-D-RUG-dplyr-II-talk</a>\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; Or clone the whole thing and build from the Rmd file in Rstudio.\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; B\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; On Sat, Feb 6, 2016 at 21:22 Danielle Hagood &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">daniell...@gmail.com</a>&gt;\r<br>&gt; wrote:\r<br>&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt; Did Brandon Hurr share his slides anywhere? I want to reference them while\r<br>&gt;&gt; playing with joins.\r<br>&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt; On Monday, February 1, 2016 at 1:28:13 PM UTC-8, Michael wrote:\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt; Hi all,\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt; Tomorrow at 3:10 in Wickson 2124, Brandon Hurr will give a talk on using\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt; dplyr’s join operations to work with related data tables. If you can’t make\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt; it in person, the talk will be livecast here. After the talk, we’ll have the\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt; usual work session until 5pm. Here is a short blurb from Brandon, and the\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt; attached script is for following along during the talk.\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt; In the real world, data is often connected, but stored in independent\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt; datasets (tables). Join operations in dplyr mimic those in SQL and allow\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt; multiple table integration and filtering. I will introduce you to these\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt; operations, and show you how to use them with examples (attached).\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt; See you tomorrow,\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt; Michael\r<br>&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt; --\r<br>&gt;&gt; Check out our R resources at\r<br>&gt;&gt; <a href=\"http://www.noamross.net/davis-r-users-group.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.noamross.net/davis-r-users-group.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792467557197000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0C-GNC60GUVr9ALVuWxgKi\">http://www.noamross.net/davis-r-users-group.html</a>\r<br>&gt;&gt; ---\r<br>&gt;&gt; You received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups\r<br>&gt;&gt; &quot;Davis R Users&#39; Group&quot; group.\r<br>&gt;&gt; To unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an\r<br>&gt;&gt; email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">davis-rug+...@googlegroups.com</a>.\r<br>&gt;&gt; Visit this group at <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/group/davis-rug\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/group/davis-rug&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792467557197000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3j_n78jYkGBUzJbCoYRFt3\">https://groups.google.com/group/davis-rug</a>.\r<br>&gt;&gt; For more options, visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/optout\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/optout&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792467557197000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1n0MKh1cBca8nV3y6GbHGa\">https://groups.google.com/d/optout</a>.\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; --\r<br>&gt; Check out our R resources at\r<br>&gt; <a href=\"http://www.noamross.net/davis-r-users-group.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.noamross.net/davis-r-users-group.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792467557197000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0C-GNC60GUVr9ALVuWxgKi\">http://www.noamross.net/davis-r-users-g